Subject: [PATCH 08147/11362] [outer-loop] Restore 34 determinations erased for
 the SECOND time; clear the freshness debt my own change created

TWO FINDINGS, both corrections owed rather than formalities.

1. THE PREMISE WAS BACKWARDS. artifact_freshness_lint.py was NOT red at pristine HEAD
   with pre-existing debt. It was GREEN. Recorded dependency hashes do not match HEAD
   (recorded cf34e53f/d3401dfd vs HEAD 8406b89a), but every one of those drifts was
   already covered by a freshness_acknowledgements block pinning HEAD's exact hash. A
   first analysis that ignored the acknowledgement mechanism reported "11 pre-existing
   stale artifacts"; re-run with the lint's own ack logic it is 0. Every one of the 12
   stale reports was caused by THIS session's staged edits to four modules -- so this
   is not inherited debt, it is my change paying for itself.

2. A TEST RUN ERASED 34 DETERMINATIONS, AGAIN. Conductor commit 4b7c813d28 ran
   `git add -A` after a pytest child rewrote tracked results/** in place; 7 artifacts
   lost 27 determination/corrigendum keys, incl. 6 `flagged_adversarial` quarantine
   stamps and exp3946's `solve_provenance`. Six still carried a
   flagged_adversarial_restoration_note from 2026-07-27 -- the same records, destroyed
   a second time. Dropping a stamp RE-ADMITS a quarantined artifact to headline
   aggregation, so this is a live correctness risk, not bookkeeping. Restored
   byte-identical to 509b3ed0e8; the conductor's MEASUREMENT values are kept
   (fail-forward). Verified strictly additive: dropped=0, changed=0 on all 7.

WHY ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS AND NOT 12 REBUILDS. A rebuild was tried first, on the cheapest
artifact: arc_gateway_card_ground_truth_20260727.json, 374.2s, 48/48 cells, 6 games x 3
seeds replayed through E3AgentPolicy. NO SCIENTIFIC FIGURE MOVED -- the verdict still
reads real_median_optimism 0.018097 vs modelled 0.036903, model wrong on 17 of 44
cells, 6 sign-flipped, and every per-cell off/res/card/real/m2/repro value was
identical. The only deltas were 48 wall-clock timings, provenance hashes and the
checksum. But the rebuild also SILENTLY DROPPED all 5 pre-existing acknowledgement
blocks (33 keys) -- a never-prune violation executed by the rebuild tooling. That
rebuild was reverted. Repeating it 11 more times would have rewritten hundreds of
published timings and destroyed ~100 hand-written records to re-prove what one rebuild
already proved. The 22 acknowledgements added here follow the precedent of the 5 prior
default-OFF changes to this same file, each cleared the same way.

The rebuild tooling dropping freshness_acknowledgements is a real defect and is filed
here rather than fixed, because fixing it belongs with whoever owns the analyser.

Each acknowledgement pins the exact new hash, so it expires the moment the file changes
again. Inertness argued per module: agent = one default-OFF branch; trust_energy =
additive, gated call site; executable_world_model = observation-only counters, zero
lines removed; experiment_5760 = whitelist widened to stop dropping keys. Backed by 55
tests passing in BOTH flag directions with trajectory-invariance for OFF.

